 "best_idea": "Pick walk or run from hysteresis over a smoothed speed (enter 5.2, leave 3.6, 0.25 s dwell) and latch moving for 0.22 s after a speed dip, so noisy frames never flip the clip; then match each gait's playback rate to speed within clamps and crossfade with a length that depends on whether water is involved.",
 "decision": "adapt",
 "decision_why": "Frankendom's hero needs the same latch and walk/run dwell so its clips do not flicker; the thresholds and reference speeds are the donor's and must become per-hero data set from Frankendom's own speeds; the rig-only hitstop is a visual shape only and sits with row 10.",
 "decision_status": "proposed",
